 <p>When marked with =93sei=94, a metalinguistic utterance can be embedded =
in another utterance as a discursive. In this way, discursives which do not=
 have cmavo assigned in selma'o UI can be expressed:</p>
 <pre>
 <a id=3D"e3" name=3D"e3">12.3)</a>  la frank. prami sei la frank. gleki la=
 djein.
        Frank loves (Frank is happy) Jane.
 </pre>
 Using the happiness attitudinal, =93.ui=94, would imply that the speaker w=
as happy. Instead, the speaker attributes happiness to Frank. It would prob=
ably be safe to elide the one who is happy, and say:
 <pre>
 <a id=3D"e4" name=3D"e4">12.4)</a>  la frank. prami sei gleki la djein.
        Frank loves (he is happy) Jane.
 </pre>
-The grammar of the bridi following =93sei=94 has an unusual limitation: th=
